# Specialist entities and derived information

A shared visual language must not flatten different evidence into the same “healthy” badge. Entity platforms define capabilities; their integrations determine available values and meaning. The coverage inventory enumerates all 45 Core entity platforms, plus separate helper/state domains. It does not claim that every integration exposes identical fields or even a dashboard control.

<h2 id="environment">Plant, environmental and derived observations</h2>

Plant status can combine moisture, light, temperature or conductivity readings and configured thresholds. Identify the specific reading outside its configured range; do not diagnose a plant from an icon. A missing measurement must stay missing. A threshold set by the household is not a professional recommendation.

Air-quality and sensor entities can report several different quantities with different units. Show the supplied quantity, value, observation context and any source-defined scale. Do not apply a generic percentage or a medical “safe” claim. Binary sensor states depend on device class: contact open, moisture detected and battery low are different meanings, not interchangeable red/green statuses.

Sun information is calculated for the configured location and time. An elevation or next-rise time is a prediction/calculation, not a brightness sensor reading. Calendar and weather predictions similarly retain their own source and period. Keep the [weather contract](weather-and-warnings.html) and [time contract](locale-units-and-time.html) authoritative for those families.

