<h2 id="events">Events, locations and image processing</h2>

An event records something that happened. It is not necessarily a state that remains true until another event. Show its type and recorded time without inventing duration. A geolocation entity marks a location supplied by an integration; a device tracker or person has different identity and privacy semantics. Follow [maps and zones](maps-and-zones.html) and [presence](presence-and-privacy.html#ha-ctrl-014-states) instead of treating every point as a person currently present.

An image entity is an image resource. Image-processing results may describe a particular image, scan time and detected objects. Keep those together; a retained detection is not proof that an object remains present. Display confidence only when supplied and meaningful for that model, with its documented interpretation. Avoid faces, names or other personal details on shared displays unless the actual permission boundary allows them.

