<h2 id="generated">AI, voice and generated output</h2>

AI task, conversation, Assist satellite, speech-to-text, text-to-speech and wake-word platforms participate in different stages. A wake-word event is not a transcript; a transcript is not an accepted command; generated text is not a verified device result. Preserve the chosen provider, pipeline and native consent/account boundaries.

Treat generated output as untrusted content for display. Label a generated suggestion and any stated limitations, provide the original relevant device evidence, and require the native action/permission flow before work is requested. Never promote a model's confident sentence to a safety assessment or a confirmed household state. A failed speech step should offer a supported typed or visual route rather than repeatedly listening without explanation. See [Assist and voice](assist-and-voice.html).

