<h2 id="fallback">Unknown domains and future integrations</h2>

Prefer native default information when a platform has no dedicated control. Show identity, the correctly formatted state and available attributes with clear labels; retain an unresolved-state explanation where necessary. Do not infer actions from a friendly name, an icon, an integration name or an arbitrary attribute called “status”. Radio/infrared/remote operations follow [helper and operation guidance](helpers-and-scalar-inputs.html#operations); notify follows [notification delivery](notifications-and-delivery.html).

New custom integrations and custom cards require their own capability and implementation review. The finite official platform list cannot establish their support. Register a reviewed extension separately rather than silently counting it as a built-in component.

<h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance checks</h2>

Test a threshold breach with a second missing reading, a retained image result, an event with no end time, calculated sun data and generated text contradicting device evidence. Confirm all timestamps and units retain their meaning. Check that viewing generated suggestions makes no device request and that private location/image details are not exposed through supposedly decorative labels or alternative text.

Sources: [Entities and domains](https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/configuration/entities_domains/), [Plant](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/plant/), [Air quality](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/air_quality/), [Event](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/event/), [Sun](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/sun/), [AI task](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/ai_task/), and the [Core 2026.11.1 platform registry](https://github.com/home-assistant/core/blob/d8a0dc698c8946b44e455d904000db563cfbf1ba/homeassistant/generated/entity_platforms.py).

<h2 id="evidence">Implementation and evidence boundary</h2>

This is a reference design specification, not a replacement for native Home Assistant components. The examples use invented records and local draft feedback; they do not call Home Assistant. Mapping a registry entry here establishes a design owner, not proof that every integration, browser or device has been tested. Keep native state formatting, translations, permissions, capabilities and event handling. Theme tokens can change presentation; they cannot supply missing application behaviour.

The [interface coverage inventory](../reference/ha-interface-coverage.json) records the finite source baseline and exact mappings. Recheck native behaviour after frontend changes. Use the [native task acceptance process](native-task-accessibility.html) to record what was actually tested.

Apply the [design styles](../styles/index.html), [writing guide](../content/index.html), [layout](../styles/layout.html), [colour roles](../styles/colour.html) and [typography](../styles/typography.html). Structural dividers use the quiet border token; editable boundaries and focus indicators remain distinct. Preserve 16px native control text, visible labels, keyboard access and readable names at 320px. A compact arrangement must not remove a capability explanation or essential recovery route.

